{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"variadic-templates","title":"Variadic Templates & Fold Expressions","group":"Templates & Generic Programming","order":44,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A <em>parameter pack</em> (<code>typename... Args</code>) lets a template accept any number of arguments of any types — how <code>std::make_unique</code>, <code>std::tuple</code> and <code>emplace_back</code> work.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-sum\"></i>Fold expressions (C++17)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\ntemplate &lt;typename... Ts&gt;\nauto sum(Ts... xs) { return (xs + ... + 0); }            // binary right fold with init 0\n\ntemplate &lt;typename... Ts&gt;\nvoid printAll(const Ts&amp;... xs) {\n    ((std::cout &lt;&lt; xs &lt;&lt; ' '), ...);                     // unary fold over the comma operator\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; \"(\" &lt;&lt; sizeof...(xs) &lt;&lt; \" args)\\n\";    // number of elements in the pack\n}\n\ntemplate &lt;typename... Ts&gt;\nbool allPositive(Ts... xs) { return ((xs &gt; 0) &amp;&amp; ...); }\n\nint main() {\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; sum(1, 2, 3, 4) &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; sum() &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; sum(1.5, 2) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    printAll(1, \"two\", 3.0, std::string(\"four\"), 'v');\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; allPositive(1, 5, 9) &lt;&lt; allPositive(1, -5) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 0 3.5\n1 two 3 four v (5 args)\n10</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Fold</th><th>Expands to</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>(pack op ...)</code></td><td><code>x1 op (x2 op (x3 op x4))</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>(... op pack)</code></td><td><code>((x1 op x2) op x3) op x4</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>(pack op ... op init)</code></td><td><code>x1 op (x2 op (… op init))</code> — works for an empty pack</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-recycle\"></i>Recursive style (pre-C++17)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n\nvoid logAll() { std::cout &lt;&lt; '\\n'; }                 // base case: empty pack\n\ntemplate &lt;typename T, typename... Rest&gt;\nvoid logAll(const T&amp; first, const Rest&amp;... rest) {  // peel off one argument per call\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; '[' &lt;&lt; first &lt;&lt; ']';\n    logAll(rest...);                              // pack expansion\n}\n\nint main() { logAll(\"id\", 42, 3.5); }</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[id][42][3.5]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-forward\"></i>Forwarding a pack</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;memory&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;utility&gt;\n\nstruct User {\n    std::string name;\n    int age;\n    User(std::string n, int a) : name(std::move(n)), age(a) {}\n};\n\ntemplate &lt;typename T, typename... Args&gt;\nstd::unique_ptr&lt;T&gt; create(Args&amp;&amp;... args) {                    // a hand-written make_unique\n    return std::unique_ptr&lt;T&gt;(new T(std::forward&lt;Args&gt;(args)...));\n}\n\nint main() {\n    auto u = create&lt;User&gt;(\"Ada\", 36);\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; u-&gt;name &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; u-&gt;age &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Ada 36</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What does sizeof...(args) return?</summary><div><p>The number of elements in the parameter pack, as a compile-time constant. It doesn't evaluate the arguments or measure their byte sizes.</p></div></details></section>"}